1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,840
A tuition centre finds its fee spreadsheet, with parents' IC numbers and a child's allergy,

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,890
posted in a public Facebook group.

3
00:00:07,890 --> 00:00:13,020
Under Malaysia's data protection law, it now has 72 hours to notify the Commissioner.

4
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:18,820
The tempting shortcut is to paste the list into a chatbot and ask what to do.

5
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:23,840
That uploads everyone's personal data a second time. Lapor72 does the opposite.

6
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:30,140
This is Lapor72, live in Chrome on a MacBook Air. The owner pastes the leaked rows.

7
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:35,860
Gemini Nano reads them on this laptop, through Firebase AI Logic in only-on-device mode,

8
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,830
together with rules for Malaysian IC, phone and bank formats.

9
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:42,660
Every finding shows its evidence,

10
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:46,740
and the step log shows it ran on the device with no internet requests.

11
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:51,050
The model flagged addresses that are not there, so the owner unticks them,

12
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,090
and adds the unpaid fees it missed.

13
00:00:53,990 --> 00:00:56,690
Next, a few questions about what happened.

14
00:00:56,690 --> 00:01:01,450
Lapor72 applies the Commissioner's breach notification tests. Health data,

15
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:07,170
financial details and IC numbers mean both the Commissioner and the parents must be told,

16
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:09,610
and the clock shows the real deadline.

17
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:15,090
Before anything leaves, Gemini Nano finds names in the owner's own answers,

18
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:17,730
and the rules remove phone numbers and IDs.

19
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:21,150
A final check blocks the send if anything slips through.

20
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:23,960
The owner sees exactly what goes to the cloud.

21
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:27,720
Only that redacted fact sheet goes to cloud Gemini,

22
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:30,190
which drafts the notice to the Commissioner,

23
00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:33,160
and the parents' notice in English and Bahasa Melayu.

24
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:36,080
The contact person's name is put back on the device,

25
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:39,380
and the case is saved to Firestore without the leaked data.

26
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:46,270
We measured it. On 20 held-out synthetic records in English, Malay, Chinese and mixed text,

27
00:01:46,270 --> 00:01:52,180
on-device Gemini Nano with rules found every kind of personal data, matching cloud Gemini,

28
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:56,850
in about 1.25 seconds. So there is no accuracy reason to upload a leak.

29
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:02,310
Each step has its own inference mode. App Check protects the cloud calls.

30
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:07,500
Remote Config holds the model name and the legal thresholds. The app works offline,

31
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:12,430
and browsers without an on-device model see a clearly labelled recorded result.

32
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:21,860
Lapor72. 72 hours, and the leaked records never leave your device. Try it at lapor72.web.app
